<title>UK: Glaxo dips amid talk of broker downgrade.</title>
<headline>Glaxo dips amid talk of broker downgrade.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in pharmaceutical company Glaxo Wellcome slipped on Thursday amid talk that analysts at HSBC James Capel had downgraded its earnings forecasts.</p>
<p>The shares fell 5-1/2p to 932-1/2p in active trade.</p>
<p>Analysts at the brokerage were unavailable for immediate comment but traders said forecasts were cut to reflect the recent strengthening of the pound.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4027</p>
</text>
